<p:sld xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main" xmlns:r="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships" xmlns:p="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/presentationml/2006/main"><p:cSld><p:spTree><p:nvGrpSpPr><p:cNvPr id="1" name=""><a:extLst><a:ext uri="{FF2B5EF4-FFF2-40B4-BE49-F238E27FC236}"><a16:creationId xmlns:a16="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2014/main" id="{D6D49771-4FDF-F89C-3F0B-E19E2DE76227}"/></a:ext></a:extLst></p:cNvPr><p:cNvGrpSpPr/><p:nvPr/></p:nvGrpSpPr><p:grpSpPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="0" y="0"/><a:ext cx="0" cy="0"/><a:chOff x="0" y="0"/><a:chExt cx="0" cy="0"/></a:xfrm></p:grpSpPr><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="4" name="Title 3"><a:extLst><a:ext uri="{FF2B5EF4-FFF2-40B4-BE49-F238E27FC236}"><a16:creationId xmlns:a16="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2014/main" id="{B77ED2DA-E456-8C9E-7246-0CB2C0A26A40}"/></a:ext></a:extLst></p:cNvPr><p:cNvSpPr><a:spLocks noGrp="1"/></p:cNvSpPr><p:nvPr><p:ph type="title"/></p:nvPr></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr/><p:txBody><a:bodyPr/><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" dirty="0"/><a:t>TESTING A SIGA-</a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" dirty="0" err="1"/><a:t>ddos</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr lang="en-US" dirty="0"/></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="5" name="Content Placeholder 4"><a:extLst><a:ext uri="{FF2B5EF4-FFF2-40B4-BE49-F238E27FC236}"><a16:creationId xmlns:a16="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2014/main" id="{3C723DB4-CAED-16A0-AED2-2504BA622BF9}"/></a:ext></a:extLst></p:cNvPr><p:cNvSpPr><a:spLocks noGrp="1"/></p:cNvSpPr><p:nvPr><p:ph sz="half" idx="1"/></p:nvPr></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="1447330" y="2010878"/><a:ext cx="9605635" cy="4125517"/></a:xfrm></p:spPr><p:txBody><a:bodyPr><a:normAutofit/></a:bodyPr><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:pPr marL="342900" indent="-342900"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="100000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="600"/></a:spcBef><a:buFont typeface="+mj-lt"/><a:buAutoNum type="arabicPeriod"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1600" dirty="0"/><a:t>Put the duct smoke detector in Fast Test mode by doing one of the following: </a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr lvl="1"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="100000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="600"/></a:spcBef></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1400" dirty="0"/><a:t>On the front of the duct smoke detector, hold an SD-MAG test magnet where indicated for between 5 and 10 seconds. </a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr lvl="1"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="100000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="600"/></a:spcBef></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1400" dirty="0"/><a:t>On an SD-TRK, turn the key switch to the TEST position for between 5 and 10 seconds. </a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr lvl="1"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="100000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="600"/></a:spcBef></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1400" dirty="0"/><a:t>On an SD-TRM, hold the SD-MAG test magnet to the target area for between 5 and 10 seconds. Holding the test magnet or the key switch for more than 10 second puts the duct smoke detector into the alarm state without testing whether the smoke sensing chamber is working. </a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="342900" indent="-342900"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="100000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="600"/></a:spcBef><a:buFont typeface="+mj-lt"/><a:buAutoNum type="arabicPeriod"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1600" dirty="0"/><a:t>Once the Test indicator starts blinking, spray a 5-second burst of canned smoke into the air duct about two feet upstream from the detector. </a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="342900" indent="-342900"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="100000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="600"/></a:spcBef><a:buFont typeface="+mj-lt"/><a:buAutoNum type="arabicPeriod"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1600" dirty="0"/><a:t>Once the detector is activated, verify the following: </a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr lvl="1"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="100000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="600"/></a:spcBef></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1400" dirty="0"/><a:t>The detector’s red Alarm indicator is flashing </a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr lvl="1"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="100000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="600"/></a:spcBef></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1400" dirty="0"/><a:t>The appropriate event message or visual indication is reported on the fire alarm system’s LCD user interface </a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr lvl="1"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="100000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="600"/></a:spcBef></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1400" dirty="0"/><a:t>If connected, the red Alarm indicator on the remote test station or on the remote alarm indicator is flashing </a:t></a:r></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp></p:spTree><p:extLst><p:ext uri="{BB962C8B-B14F-4D97-AF65-F5344CB8AC3E}"><p14:creationId xmlns:p14="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/powerpoint/2010/main" val="3221210683"/></p:ext></p:extLst></p:cSld><p:clrMapOvr><a:masterClrMapping/></p:clrMapOvr></p:sld>